## Streaming

Two Forter surfaces stream responses using **Server-Sent Events (SSE)**:

- **MCP server (demo)** at [www.forter.com/mcp](https://www.forter.com/mcp)
  and **production** at [mcp.forter.com/mcp](https://mcp.forter.com/mcp) -
  both use the MCP **Streamable HTTP** transport, which streams JSON-RPC
  responses to the agent as `text/event-stream` when a long-running
  `tools/call` needs to emit progress before the final result.
- **NLWeb `/ask`** endpoint at [www.forter.com/ask](https://www.forter.com/ask)
  - returns `Content-Type: text/event-stream` when the request signals a
  streaming preference (`?streaming=true`, a body `streaming` flag, a
  nested `{"prefer":{"streaming":true}}`, a `Prefer: streaming=true`
  header, or `Accept: text/event-stream`). NLWeb event types: `start`,
  `result`, `complete`.

The **REST API** at `api.forter-secure.com` is synchronous request /
response - real-time decisioning typically returns in under 100ms, so
streaming is not used there. Clients should set a ~2 s timeout and retry
once on `5xx` / `429` with exponential backoff.

